Overlay patch 0026: the engine boots once per process, period.
visionOS scene reconnects (window-resize stress) re-invoked the process
entry and re-ran the game's main() in-process — through MORE than one
UIKit path: a postFinishLaunch-level guard (0021 rev4) shipped and was
bypassed (device log: two "Starting Ship of Harkinian" inits 55 s apart
with the Console singleton alive across them). Guard at the chokepoint
every path must cross: soh's main(). The shell separately re-attaches
the existing SDL window to a reconnected scene.

--- a/soh/src/code/main.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/main.c
@@ -58,6 +58,19 @@
 #else //_WIN32
 int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
 #endif
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0026): visionOS scene reconnects re-invoke the
+     * process entry through multiple UIKit paths; a second in-process boot
+     * restarts the game from the intro and leaves twin audio threads racing
+     * one device. The engine boots once per process, ever. */
+    {
+        static int sohIosMainRan = 0;
+        if (sohIosMainRan) {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        sohIosMainRan = 1;
+    }
+#endif
     GameConsole_Init();
     InitOTR(argc, argv);
     // TODO: Was moved to below InitOTR because it requires window to be setup. But will be late to catch crashes.
